  "reason": "Retain prior project lifecycle, chat rewind, Notebook edit, transcript export, product knowledge, registry, and typed-action selections. Cover exact shared Library catalog and revision guards, browser-owned file selection and original-file download, reindex and removal, artifact retention, background exclusion, product-help discovery, and receipt parsing. Four frontend files collect 75 cases for Butler browser handoffs and previous project/export behavior. Eight paired non-loopback LAN Library profiles cover cancellation, authenticated upload, original-byte download, revision guard, read-back, refresh, reconnect, removal, and retained artifact journey in addition to the prior 32 cases.",
  "exclusions": "No native source changed, so no native tests are selected. Unrelated Python, frontend and browser journeys are excluded. Notebook run lifecycle/package installation, workspace files, browser/research data, and other audited operator controls still require separate work. Browser profiles emulate mobile devices; physical Safari and the operating system's final download save location are unavailable. Butler's enabled Knowledge setting may separately supply bounded Library excerpts to the model; the control action sends metadata only. A confirmed Library removal proves the Core item is absent and the original artifact remains; it does not independently prove every downstream index cache is cleared after an index cleanup failure.",
